<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Southern Bug</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hypanis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Southern Bug is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> that flows about 800 km south-east from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/podolia">Podolia</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>, entering the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a>–Bug estuary near Mykolaiv. Known to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> as the Hypanis, it gave the Milesian colony of Olbia on its estuary access to the steppe. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it bounded Podolia, contested by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/southern-bug.jpg" alt="Southern Bug" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Chernilevsky · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunset_S_Bug_Vinnitsa_2007_G1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
